# Dreierschnapsen Project Rules

## Architecture

- Three-crate Cargo workspace: `schnapsen-model`, `schnapsen-engine`, `schnapsen-cli`
- `schnapsen-model` is the core dependency — never import engine/cli types into it
- Game state is immutable-style: `GameState::apply_action()` mutates in place but validates first

## Domain Terminology

Use consistent naming for game concepts:

| German | English (code) | Description |
|--------|----------------|-------------|
| Rufer | `rufer` | Caller — determines trump, sits left of dealer |
| Geber | `geber` | Dealer |
| Trumpf/Atout | `trump` | Trump suit |
| Farb- und Stichzwang | suit+trump obligation | Must follow suit, must beat, must trump |
| Zwanziger | `Marriage` (non-trump) | King+Queen of same suit = 20 pts |
| Vierziger | `Marriage` (trump) | King+Queen of trump suit = 40 pts |
| Bummerl | `bummerl` | Loss marker in match scoring |
| Spritzen | `SpritzenLevel` | Doubling mechanism (×2, ×4, ×8) |
| Talon | `talon` | 2 face-down cards in the middle |

## Card Model

- 4 suits: Hearts, Diamonds, Spades, Clubs
- 5 ranks per suit: Ace(11), Ten(10), King(4), Queen(3), Jack(2)
- 20 cards total, 120 points total in deck
- Multiple rank orderings exist (standard, ace-low, ten-low, king-low)

## Code Conventions

- Use `PlayerId` (usize 0..3) for player identification
- `Card::new(suit, rank)` — always construct cards this way
- `valid_plays()` and `trick_winner()` are pure functions in `types.rs`
- `GameState` is the single source of truth for a hand's state
- All game type metadata (points, trump, goal, ordering) lives on `GameType` enum methods
